{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbZZJN9VMfkCmdeSpDia", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Return an RFC 7807 `application/problem+json` response built with the `problem()` helper in `src/api/errors.py`. Don't build your own error dicts.\n\n```python\nfrom api.errors import problem\n\n@app.post(\"/refunds\")\ndef create_refund():\n    ...\n    if amount > invoice.total:\n        return problem(422, \"Refund exceeds invoice total\",\n                       detail=f\"Requested {amount}, invoice total is {invoice.total}\")\n```\n\nThe helper (`src/api/errors.py:4`):\n- returns the body `{\"type\": \"about:blank\", \"title\": ..., \"status\": ...}`, and adds `detail` only when you pass one;\n- sets the HTTP status code on the response to match `status`;\n- sets the content type to `application/problem+json`.\n\n**Where this comes from:**\n- **The helper itself.** It's the only error-response code in the API layer.\n- **A team memory.** The project's EngramDB memory store has a note written by a person (\"API errors use problem+json\", scoped to `src/api/`) that sets this as the rule: use `errors.problem(status, title, detail)` and \"do not return ad-hoc dicts.\"\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Domain errors need converting.** Code in `src/billing/` raises ordinary Python exceptions, for example `ValueError(\"refund exceeds invoice total\")` in `refunds.py:6`. I didn't find a Flask error handler that turns these into problem responses. As things stand, your endpoint has to catch them and return `problem(...)` itself, or someone has to add an `@app.errorhandler` that calls `problem()`.\n- **The memory search came back empty.** A ranked EngramDB search for \"API endpoint error response convention\" returned no results, even though that memory's file is in `.engramdb/memories/`. I found it by reading the file directly. The search index may be out of date, and running EngramDB's `reindex` might fix it. I haven't run it because it changes the store."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 843, "cache_read_input_tokens": 21677, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 843}, "output_tokens": 4, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "903f6cdc-dba8-4f3c-9bdb-74e62e7710b2", "uuid": "0b270672-a064-43f6-8ef9-9bcb7f4a4b93", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:02:40.104Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbZZHzpqf9cudB2ZMbqU"}
